      "body": "## Summary\n\nFixes #43882.\n\nThe Rust normalizer (`normalize_bootstrap_columns`) uses `wrapping_add` to fan out a scalar `bootstrap_room` across a batch, while the Python normalizer (`io_struct.py`) uses arbitrary-precision addition. For rooms near `i64::MAX` the two frontends derive different room values for the same request body, breaking the PD rendezvous contract — the prefill and decode legs rendezvous on different rooms and the KV transfer times out.\n\n## Change\n\nReject with `Error::Validation` when `room > i64::MAX - (prompt_count - 1)` — exactly the condition under which `wrapping_add` would wrap and diverge from Python. The boundary room `i64::MAX - (prompt_count - 1)` is still accepted (its fan-out reaches exactly `i64::MAX` without wrapping).\n\n- `prompt_count >= 1` is guaranteed by `into_requests` (empty batches are rejected), so the subtraction cannot underflow.\n- The `wrapping_add` fan-out is unchanged for accepted rooms, preserving distinct pairing keys.\n- Python is unchanged: its arbitrary-precision semantics are the correct reference.\n\n## Test\n\n`bootstrap_room_fan_out_overflow_rejected`:\n- scalar room `i64::MAX` with 2 prompts → rejected with a Validation error naming `bootstrap_room`\n- boundary room `i64::MAX - 1` with 2 prompts → accepted with rooms `[MAX-1, MAX]`\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38294536810](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38294536810)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38294536268](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38294536268)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:heavy_minus_sign: **No AMD PR run found for this commit**.<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
